#include \(dqbashclient.h\(dq

bc_client_t *bc_connect(const char *socket_path);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Establishes a connection to a running \f[CR]bash\-server(1)\f[R]
instance through a Unix domain socket.
The function creates a \f[CR]SOCK_STREAM\f[R] socket, connects to the
path specified by \f[CR]socket_path\f[R], and returns an opaque client
handle suitable for use with \f[CR]bc_auth(3)\f[R],
\f[CR]bc_eval(3)\f[R], and other API functions.
.PP
The returned handle must eventually be released with
\f[CR]bc_close(3)\f[R].
.PP
If \f[CR]socket_path\f[R] is NULL, the function attempts to resolve the
server socket using the standard search order:
.IP "1." 3
\f[CR]$BASH_SERVER_SOCKET\f[R] environment variable
.IP "2." 3
\f[CR]\(ti/.bash\-serverrc\f[R] configuration file
.IP "3." 3
\f[CR]$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bash\-server/sock\f[R]
.IP "4." 3
\f[CR]/tmp/bash\-server\-<uid>/sock\f[R]
.PP
After a successful connection, the caller must authenticate with
\f[CR]bc_auth(3)\f[R] before issuing any commands.
