.SH ERRORS
The function may fail when:
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]socket_path\f[R] exceeds the maximum length for a Unix domain
socket address (\f[CR]sizeof(struct sockaddr_un.sun_path) \- 1\f[R],
typically 107 bytes).
.IP \(bu 2
The socket file does not exist or the server is not running.
.IP \(bu 2
The calling process lacks permission to access the socket file.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]malloc(3)\f[R] fails to allocate the client handle.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]socket(2)\f[R] or \f[CR]connect(2)\f[R] fails for any
system\-level reason.
.IP \(bu 2
