.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The client handle is not thread\-safe.
Each thread should use its own connection.
.IP \(bu 2
The function performs a blocking \f[CR]connect(2)\f[R] call.
If the server accept queue is full, the call may block until a slot is
available or the connection is refused.
.IP \(bu 2
The maximum socket path length is determined by \f[CR]sun_path\f[R] in
\f[CR]struct sockaddr_un\f[R], which is typically 108 bytes (107 usable
characters plus the NUL terminator) on Linux/Cygwin.
.IP \(bu 2
After \f[CR]bc_connect\f[R] returns successfully, the connection is in
an unauthenticated state.
All commands except \f[CR]bc_auth(3)\f[R] will fail with
\f[CR]BC_ERR_AUTH\f[R] until authentication succeeds.
.IP \(bu 2
The caller is responsible for ensuring the server is running before
calling \f[CR]bc_connect\f[R].
Use \f[CR]bc_connect_stdio(3)\f[R] to automatically launch a server
subprocess.
